    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "When I turn your head to the right, your eyes flick sideways, that's called nystagmus.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:00",
      "end_timestamp": "04:07",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good, that's the examination. Having listened and examined, it's hard to say. Benign positional vertigo is one possibility and a migraine-related dizziness another, and I'd rather not commit yet.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:10",
      "end_timestamp": "04:22",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "clinical_assessment[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now benign positional vertigo is my leading thought, not anything worse. A hearing test is what I'd like next, for tinnitus and vertigo get up slowly from lying down and sit for a moment first",
      "start_timestamp": "04:33",
      "end_timestamp": "04:53",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
